{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>למים</b> Five times in the Masorah: דין ואידך רפאתי למים. Namely: כל צמא לכו למים. ואדיריהם שלחו צעיריהם למים. ולא צמא למים. Meaning: if they thirst for water, their mighty ones send their young ones and they find no water — לכו למים, i.e., gratitude, and they will be healed למים, and there will be neither hunger for bread nor thirst for water." "<b>העליתנו</b> Twice in the Masorah: דין, and the other: המעט כי העליתנו, in the episode of Korah's rebellion — to say that those very same people are the ones who spoke here."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "The Hebrew lists five occurrences of the phrase למים in the Masorah; the first is cited as דין ואידך רפאתי למים (likely two separate citations run together), followed by three more, but only four distinct strings appear in the text as transmitted."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:21.282924239Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}